6-2017 time  frame  i finished at the end of 2017 and it  came out at the beginning of 2018.  um and at that time i was thinking about  this series  as bringing computer science education  to emerging languages so languages that  might  not yet have good computer science books  in them now that was true at that time  in swift and so i thought okay i'm going  to be a niche i'm going to be the first  like computer science book  for swift and you know that book did  okay  and it's been it's a i think it's a  great book uh but  it turns out that there was actually a  much bigger demand  for this type of book than i thought  somebody people were looking for  something that was somewhere between  an uh you know a tutorial and a textbook  they wanted something that was more  approachable  that was broad that that dipped into a  lot of different computer science topics  correctly  importantly of course verified by  technical reviewers and a real public  great real publisher like manning  but they didn't want something that's as  boring and and you know uh  hard to get through as a textbook and so  the publisher said to me after we did  the swift book which was you know the  swift book was pretty successful they  said  we got to bring this to a much bigger  audience and so  then we did the the python book and the  python book has just been really  successful  it's been a bestseller for manning it's  been translated now into seven different  human languages that came out at the  beginning of 2019  and so we see that there's really a  demand in um the large languages  like the popular the really popular  languages uh to have a book like this  and so we're actually porting the book  next to java i'm working on that right  now  because we're doing just the next like  really big language right and we did a  poll of our readers we said  do you want the book in um we've done  the book in swift  we're doing it in python this was back  in the beginning of 2019  do you want the book n